{
  "about": "Shared byte for byte by the R and Python suites of scopusflow. standard and complete are one synthetic Search API record as the STANDARD and the COMPLETE view return it. Nothing in it came from Scopus. Its DOI sits on the reserved 10.5555 prefix, which never resolves, and its PubMed identifier lies beyond the range PubMed has issued. Its ISSN, 00368075, begins with zeros, which a CSV reader that infers types would drop. Both views carry the document type, source type, volume, issue, pages, ISSN, PubMed identifier and open-access status, and only COMPLETE carries the abstract, as Elsevier's Search views table lists them. pybliometrics holds, for each view, the fields of pybliometrics' Document that the Python twin reads, as pybliometrics builds them from the entry. expected holds, for each view, the row both twins return with fields = \"extended\" for the query given, column by column and in order.",
